{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/590924-overlapping-gifts-at-character-creation","id":590924,"title":"Overlapping gifts at character creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-14T22:53:46-07:00","id":590924,"title":"Overlapping gifts at character creation","content":"As there are some overlaps between auspices and tribes with starting affinity Gifts does anyone give their players something to equal it out so that no character creation choice has a mechanical advantage over another? (eg when the character opens up a Gift for the overlapping one they get two initial facets instead of one, experience break of two points on something else instead, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:40:22-07:00","id":590968,"title":"","content":"Literally no combination of tribal and auspice affinities exists that produces a low enough total that you can't get at least two uses out of your affinity cost-break after the starting distribution of two Shadow Facets, and the unique tribal affinities maintain their niches no matter what auspice your character is.<br /> <br /> Whether anyone gave Ghost Wolves something to make up for the two or three lost affinities not having a tribe loses you might be a more interesting question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T06:39:12-07:00","id":591219,"title":"","content":"At most you're looking at one overlapping gift, so that &quot;mechanical advantage&quot; comes to a grand total of needing to pay two less experiences over the course of an entire chronicle, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T07:38:49-07:00","id":591291,"title":"","content":"It is only two experiences but it is still a mechanical advantage, albeit a very minor one. In any event, I'm curious if anyone has done anything. I'm also going to add on what Satchel mentioned above; has anyone given Ghost Wolves anything to make up for the lost affinities? Is there anyone running a Ghost Wolves chronicle and have you done anything to help them out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T07:47:30-07:00","id":591298,"title":"","content":"I view the issue with Ghost Wolves as the price paid for having no tribe and no tribal ban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T07:51:24-07:00","id":591302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vedic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/590924-overlapping-gifts-at-character-creation?p=591291#post591291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is only two experiences but it is still a mechanical advantage, albeit a very minor one. In any event, I'm curious if anyone has done anything. I'm also going to add on what Satchel mentioned above; has anyone given Ghost Wolves anything to make up for the lost affinities? Is there anyone running a Ghost Wolves chronicle and have you done anything to help them out?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were running a Ghost Wolf chronicle (meaning: all characters are Ghost Wolves) I wouldn't make any changes, since they're all equal with each other w.r.t. affinities and experience.<br /> <br /> If I was running a game with Forsaken and Ghost Wolves, I'd probably give the Ghost Wolf PCs the cost of a Renown in XP and say that if they want to buy a renown with it then they need to perform a renown deed in-game as usual.<br /> <br /> As for the lack of gifts, they're still gonna have to go find a spirit to bestow the gift on them as usual, but since they'll have two gifts unlocked like everybody else it shouldn't be a big problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T08:51:57-07:00","id":591380,"title":"","content":"I have given an extra Shadow Gift at character creation (to everyone) and that more or less smooths it out. Basically, you get three Shadow Facets and either two Moon Facets or one Moon Facet and one Wolf Facet, depending on your starting Renown. Ghost Wolves get two Shadow Shadow Facets, one Moon Facet, and one Wolf Facet.<br /> <br /> You still <i>technically</i> save 1 experience by not taking two dots in your Auspice Renown this way, but nobody loses out on any of their free Facets, which to me is more important. And it makes the character creation rules for Renown and Gifts match up with the way it works after character creation.<br /> <br /> As an added bonus, it's the kind of house rule that's really easy to convince most players to go for, because it makes their characters more powerful out of the gate, at no cost to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-15-2015, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}